course: dictionary
lesson: 868
title: Bilingual
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bilingual means able to speak two languages well. Look at the brackets in the example: «Many people in the world grow up bilingual (speaking two languages) or multilingual (speaking several).» The brackets give you the meaning, so you can check it yourself.
explain: Bilingual can describe things as well as people. In Canada, signs are bilingual, so they are written in two languages, English and French. A bilingual dictionary has words in two languages. The word after bilingual tells you what kind of thing it describes.
explain: Look at the start of the word. Bi means two. Monolingual means one language, trilingual means three, and multilingual means many. If you know these parts, you can work out a new word before you check a dictionary.
fact: Bilingual means able to speak two languages well, or written or spoken in two languages.
fact: «A bilingual child» is a child who speaks two languages well.
fact: «Bilingual signs» are signs written in two languages, such as English and Welsh in Wales.
fact: Monolingual means one language, trilingual means three, and multilingual means several.
fact: Being bilingual is a skill, not a problem.
exercise: «Many people in the world grow up bilingual (speaking two languages).» What does bilingual mean here? | Speaking no language at all | Speaking three languages | *Speaking two languages | Speaking very loudly
exercise: In Canada, signs are bilingual. What does that mean? | Written in pictures only | Written in numbers | Written in one language only | *Written in English and French
exercise: Which word means speaking one language? | trilingual | multilingual | bilingual | *monolingual
test: Ella says a bilingual dictionary is one with pictures only. What is the right meaning? | A dictionary with words in two languages | A dictionary with numbers | *A dictionary with words in two languages, not pictures | A dictionary for one language only
test: Which word means speaking several languages? | bilingual | monolingual | *multilingual | trilingual with exactly one word
exam: «Being bilingual is a skill, not a problem.» What is the main idea? | Bilingual means speaking one language | *Bilingual people have a useful skill | Bilingual people should stop speaking one of their languages | Bilingual signs are a problem
